      "note": "Reviewed anchor call trace and receipt: a zero-value transfer to 0xd3c0e4d4ae359e0ac217f235bd46175fc60cd757 emits Transfer(pair,pair,1) at log 19; sync follows, then a 24-raw-unit sale drains USDT. Logs 8 and 30 respectively record the 2.408372926510967280 USDT input and 53200.841980198574448225 output. Complete indexed pair-overwrite history from deployment through block 121604867 has only this anchor; Pancake factory PairCreated queries with FFIST in either token position return only this pair. All 28 successful transactions in the original attacker history were traced; only the anchor touches FFIST. Full pair Swap history from anchor through block 121604867 contains 71 events. Source-4 covers 18 one-raw-unit sales by 0xd5d10c2f00c67cf215b12a34e8a282c44f200d8a returning 928.521098910126868069 USDT and 47 sales by 0xfa3146bdb434e912087691ca12c072ebe06ab232 returning 1286.151532384745338578 USDT for 7381 raw units. These sales monetise the same persistent reserve corruption; no new overwrite or age reset occurs. Every receipt reproduces the direct USDT payout. The complete incoming-USDT log query through the last sale (block 30114519) contains only the anchor purchase input, and pre-anchor USDT reserve 55420.690999928645538098 minus end-block reserve 7.584761361709850506 equals the recorded loss, excluding unrelated replenishment or liquidity withdrawal. The later 0x5c164c552942df8ff8446621a6431470d20bee17b93fb2f79ba34b78997c6477 sells an ordinary 6.152951577746875719-token balance for 7.501181716585206471 USDT, rather than tiny-unit extraction; it is excluded. The three remaining swaps purchase FFIST with USDT and add no USDT victim loss."
